  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105576",
      "title": "Understanding Generics",
      "lectureOrder": 758,
      "videoOrder": 698,
      "sourceHash": "0108bc0d49e4ed10e9f7ffbd8373c18874173bb58b975bd7c31ed6b426e42066",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.31,
          "en": "Instructor: I wanna conclude this basic introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.31,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "to TypeScript with a slightly more advanced,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 12.3,
          "en": "yet very important TypeScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.3,
          "end": 14.493,
          "en": "and that would be generics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.69,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "Now this can be tricky to wrap your head around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "but I'll try my best to explain it such that it makes sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "Let's say we have a function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 27.993,
          "en": "which I'll name insertAtBeginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.055,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "and this function takes an array and a value as parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 39.54,
          "en": "and the array should be an array full of any kinds of value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.54,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "and the value should be any kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 43.8,
          "en": "because I don't care in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "if it's an array full of numbers, or strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 48.483,
          "en": "or of person objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.35,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "Whatever it is, what I wanna do in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 54.933,
          "en": "is I wanna create a newArray,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "for example, by using the spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "and copying the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "That's a standard modern JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 68.03999999999999,
          "en": "also supported by TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.03999999999999,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "And then in front of that old array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 72.57300000000001,
          "en": "I wanna insert the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 78.753,
          "en": "And then I want to return this newArray here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "That could be a utility helper function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 84.3,
          "en": "which we create to have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "which we can easily call to add a value in an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 90.21000000000001,
          "en": "without changing the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 92.19,
          "en": "So the advantage of this function could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.19,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "that the original array never changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 97.173,
          "en": "but instead we're getting a brand new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.64,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "Now for this, I could, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 104.03999999999999,
          "en": "have a demoArray with let's say three values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 106.78,
          "en": "and then I get my updatedArray",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "where I call insertAtBeginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 112.8,
          "en": "and I pass in the demoArray,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.8,
          "end": 117.423,
          "en": "and then a value of -1, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 119.4,
          "en": "With that, I know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.4,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "that the updatedArray will be this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "with -1 inserted at the beginning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 130.07,
          "en": "so this will give me -1, 1, 2, 3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "And hence thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 133.32,
          "en": "I might wanna do things with that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.32,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "which I can do with an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.77,
          "en": "But the problem is that updatedArray, if I hover over it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 142.59,
          "en": "is inferred to be of type any array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.59,
          "end": 145.98,
          "en": "so an array full of any kind of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.98,
          "end": 148.59,
          "en": "TypeScript here doesn't pick up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.59,
          "end": 150.66,
          "en": "that it's an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 155.07,
          "en": "Why? Because here I have any as a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 158.31,
          "en": "And I can't say that I only wanna allow numbers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.31,
          "end": 161.82,
          "en": "because what if I want to use this utility function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.82,
          "end": 163.833,
          "en": "with an array full of strings?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 166.05,
          "en": "So we need any,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 168.66,
          "en": "but at the same time that kind of removes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 172.5,
          "en": "all kind of TypeScript support we might be getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.5,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "after calling this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 177.21,
          "en": "We're not getting any good TypeScript support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.21,
          "end": 179.16,
          "en": "for updatedArray after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.16,
          "end": 180.99,
          "en": "because that is inferred to be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.99,
          "end": 185.4,
          "en": "an array full of any kind of objects or any kind of values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.4,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "and that's not useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 188.55,
          "en": "If I then, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.55,
          "end": 192.36,
          "en": "try to access the first element and call split here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.36,
          "end": 196.17000000000002,
          "en": "which I could call on a string, I don't get an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 198.84,
          "en": "I would get a runtime error instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.84,
          "end": 201.48,
          "en": "because I can't call split on a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.48,
          "end": 203.52,
          "en": "But again, TypeScript doesn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.52,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "that the first value in updatedArray is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 209.22,
          "en": "We know it as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.22,
          "end": 212.76,
          "en": "but because of our type definitions here, which we need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.76,
          "end": 214.95,
          "en": "TypeScript doesn't know it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.95,
          "end": 217.11,
          "en": "And to work around such problems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 219.36,
          "en": "we have this feature of generics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.36,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "and that's why I had this lengthy introduction here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "because it is important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 227.46,
          "en": "to understand why this feature exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.46,
          "end": 229.68,
          "en": "With this generics feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.68,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "we can convert this function to a generic function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "For this, we use a special syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 240.33,
          "en": "After the function name in front of the parameter list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.33,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "we add angle brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "and that's now not a standard JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 248.19,
          "en": "but really only a feature we can use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.19,
          "end": 249.753,
          "en": "since we're using TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 254.22,
          "en": "And in here we can define a generic type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.22,
          "end": 258,
          "en": "which will only be available inside of this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 260.61,
          "en": "Typically, that's called T for type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.61,
          "end": 263.883,
          "en": "but any identifier of your choice is okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 267,
          "en": "Now you can use this type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "in your function including the parameter list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "And here I'm saying I want to use this for my array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 278.673,
          "en": "so my array will be full of Ts and my value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.26,
          "end": 282.063,
          "en": "This should always be of type T.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 283.05,
          "end": 285.03,
          "en": "But how does this help us?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 285.03,
          "end": 288.33,
          "en": "Well, like this of course is just very cryptic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.33,
          "end": 291.09000000000003,
          "en": "but now when we call this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 294.81,
          "en": "now TypeScript actually is able to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 298.26,
          "en": "that it should look at the concrete values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.26,
          "end": 300.27,
          "en": "of the arguments here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 303.21,
          "en": "and it understands that this is an array of numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 303.21,
          "end": 304.95,
          "en": "and this is just a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 306.36,
          "en": "and therefore understands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.36,
          "end": 310.05,
          "en": "that updatedArray will be an array of numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.05,
          "end": 312.54,
          "en": "because of this generic type feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.54,
          "end": 314.76,
          "en": "because we're telling TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "that the type here is actually not any type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 320.97,
          "en": "it's not any kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.97,
          "end": 325.65,
          "en": "Instead, we tell it that the type of this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 325.65,
          "end": 328.08,
          "en": "and of this value should be the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.08,
          "end": 329.64,
          "en": "just that this is an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 333,
          "en": "but it's an array full of the same types of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "as this single value has it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 338.43,
          "en": "And that's an important piece of information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.43,
          "end": 340.56,
          "en": "Therefore, TypeScript is able to look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 343.8,
          "en": "at the type of demoArray, which it knows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 343.8,
          "end": 346.38,
          "en": "It knows that this is an array of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 346.38,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "It's able to infer this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 350.25,
          "en": "And it looks at this type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 353.22,
          "en": "and then it knows that logically the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 353.22,
          "end": 356,
          "en": "which gets constructed here has to be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 356,
          "end": 358.32,
          "en": "of the same type as the input array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.32,
          "end": 360.18,
          "en": "It's able to infer this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.18,
          "end": 361.98,
          "en": "and hence it's able to infer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 361.98,
          "end": 365.97,
          "en": "that what we get back here has to be an array of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 365.97,
          "end": 370.97,
          "en": "And if I would call insert at the beginning here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 371.1,
          "end": 375.93,
          "en": "with an array of strings like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 375.93,
          "end": 378.243,
          "en": "and then pass in a string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 379.08,
          "end": 381.18,
          "en": "and I have my string array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 381.18,
          "end": 384.24,
          "en": "TypeScript is also able to infer this correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 384.24,
          "end": 385.073,
          "en": "Because again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 385.073,
          "end": 386.91,
          "en": "it looks at this type and this type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 386.91,
          "end": 389.34,
          "en": "and it knows that the return type is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 389.34,
          "end": 392.55,
          "en": "of the same value as this type, as the input array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 392.55,
          "end": 395.4,
          "en": "and hence it again infers this correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 395.4,
          "end": 397.71,
